# Data fetching

- All HTTP goes through `src/lib/apiClient.ts`. Feature files in `api/` are thin wrappers that return typed data.
- Each feature exports a `queryKeys` object. Keys include every filter that changes the result.

```typescript
export const workOrderKeys = {
  all: ["work-orders"] as const,
  detail: (id: string) => [...workOrderKeys.all, id] as const,
};

export function useWorkOrder(id: string) {
  return useQuery({
    queryKey: workOrderKeys.detail(id),
    queryFn: () => getWorkOrder(id),
  });
}
```

- Mutations invalidate the narrowest key that changed. Optimistic updates are reserved for status buttons the technician taps (`arrive`, `start`, `complete`).
- Surface `error.code` from the API in the UI. Do not match on error message text.
- Mirror API status enums in `src/lib/status.ts`. When the API adds a status, update that file in the same change.
